<title>UK: UK's Brown declines utility tax list, defines term.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown declines utility tax list, defines term.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gordon Brown, the British Labour Party's economics spokesman, declined on Tuesday to list the utilities privatised by the Conservative government which will be subject to a windfall levy to fund Labour's employment plans.</p>
<p>But he said the legislation would be &quot;non-discriminatory&quot; and the definition was clear -- all &quot;privatised utilities regulated and licensed by statute&quot;.</p>
<p>Brown added that &quot;all these utilities know exactly what their position is&quot;. He declined to say how much the tax would raise.</p>
</text>
